Subject: [PATCH] page: Fire Emblem Fates helpers: New Game defaults rows

Round 81 (docs/ROUND81_PLAN.md A1, build/r81/home/HOME_DESIGN.md; the owner's
pick F-057 #5 and its new writer group, answered "ok keep going", run on the
standing OK F-059 (3)). The words are Grok's (docs/collab/ROUND81_OPTIONS_GROK.md):
the line's name "New Game defaults" and the battle line "Off plays fights on
the map. Supports and dances follow this too."

Core (zakuro-core fates_helpers.rs, plain data, no guest access): four enums
in the EnemyPhase pattern, each with Game's choice first and default:
BattleAnimations (game / off 0 / on 1), MapSpeed (game / normal 0 / fast 1 /
fast_while_a 2), EnemySkip (game / off 0 / move 1 / all 2), HpBars (game /
off 0 / on 1); ALL, name(), key(), byte() -> Option<u8> (None = Game's
choice). Four new Helpers fields battle_animations, map_speed, enemy_skip,
hp_bars (never the unread enemy_phase). The getters the New Game writer
(patch 0040) calls, named at the top of fates_helpers.rs:
Helpers::any_new_game_row() -> bool (false = no trap word, no guest access),
Helpers::new_game_bytes() -> Vec<NewGameByte { offset, value, line_values }>
in the block's order (+0x8, +0xC, +0xD, +0x16; empty at the defaults),
Helpers::new_game_rows_set() -> usize, the row getters battle_animations(),
map_speed(), enemy_skip(), hp_bars(), and the constants
BATTLE_ANIMATIONS_OFFSET / MAP_SPEED_OFFSET / ENEMY_SKIP_OFFSET /
HP_BARS_OFFSET (0x8 / 0xC / 0xD / 0x16) and *_VALUES (5 / 3 / 3 / 2, the
game's line sizes; a value at or past one is never stored).

Settings: the four keys sit in the [fates_helpers] table, each with
skip_serializing_if at Game's choice, so an untouched file writes no table
and a round-80 file (enemy_phase, true_hit) reads and writes back byte for
byte. Every key, enemy_phase and true_hit too, is now read on its own with
fates_helpers::lenient (serde untagged Known / IgnoredAny): a value this
build does not know gives that key's default and keeps the other keys. This
changes round 80's U3 on purpose: one bad value used to reset the whole
table, True hit with it; now only that key falls back (the plan's call 7).
A table of the wrong kind (fates_helpers = 4) still gives the defaults
through or_default. One choice for Fire Emblem Fates and Seal of Flames,
as before; never a randomizer row, so no seed, answer, run id or share code
changes.

Paused window: under True hit and its help line, menus::helper_rows draws a
collapsing "New Game defaults" line (egui CollapsingHeader with the fixed id
salt "fates helpers new game", closed at first), reading "New Game defaults:
game's choice" or "New Game defaults: 2 set". Open, it shows Battle
animations, Map speed, Enemy turn skip and HP bars, each a label (help on
hover) over wrapped choices [Game's choice][...], and the note "Used when
you start a New Game. A game already going keeps its own settings; change
those on the game's Options screen. Rows that change how long things take
can make later enemy moves differ; hits, damage and the battle dice stay the
same." A change pushes Action::Settings as True hit does. Round 80's help
line is reworded to name the new row: "Faster enemy turns: set Enemy turn
skip under New Game defaults below. In a game already going, use the game's
own Options line 6 (Off, Move, or All), or press the Start key during the
enemy turn. ..." On an 800 x 480 screen the line sits just below the Paused
window's fold; the window scrolls to it (round 80's vscroll).

Page robot (pagebot.rs): targets helpers:newgame:section (always drawn for
Fates; a click opens or closes it) and, only while the line is fully open,
helpers:opt:<key>=<word> for every choice of the four rows. In
{"expect_settings": {...}} an expected "game" matches an absent key (a row
at Game's choice is not written).

Tests (cargo test --lib in the reused targets): core N1
the_new_game_rows_default_to_the_game, N2 the_choices_are_the_games_order,
N3 a_bad_word_is_the_games_choice, N4 nothing_to_store_at_the_defaults;
settings U1-U5 extended (untouched and round-80 files byte for byte, every
new value round-trips with only its key written, U3 per key now, a round-80
file has Game's choice on all four, Follow the general settings leaves
them); game_pick U6 extended (Seal shares the rows); menus U7 (closed: no
row targets; open: exactly the 14 row targets; opening saves nothing), U8
(a New Game row click saves once, the same value again nothing, Game's
choice back to the default, the line stays open while its words change),
U9 (800 x 480 and 800 x 360, closed and open, every target inside the
window's width; the test scrolls the window with the wheel to a target
below the fold), the words test; pagebot
the_robot_sets_the_new_game_rows_and_reads_them_back. zakuro-core 246
passed (engine/target/zakuro-core-test), zakuro 131 passed, 2 ignored
(engine/target/zakuro-frontend-test).

Nothing here reads or writes guest memory; with every row at Game's choice
nothing acts at all.

Repair (round 81 B2, V's R13 look at the game's own Options screen,
build/r81/review/sheet.png): two value words now match the game's screen
words. Map speed byte 2 reads "Manual" (was "Fast while A is held"; the
